      "title": "King Charles to discuss legacy of slavery with Commonwealth leaders at summit",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/28/king-charles-confirms-he-will-discuss-legacy-of-slavery-at-commonwealth-summit",
      "description": "<p>Royal tour of Caribbean comes as poll suggests majority support among younger Britons for dialogue on slavery reparations</p><p>King Charles has confirmed he will discuss the legacy of slavery at a summit with Commonwealth leaders as he begins his Caribbean tour.</p><p>The king arrived in the Bahamas on Tuesday to a ceremonial welcome and attended a youth rally at Clifford Park, the site where the country officially gained its independence from British colonial rule in 1973.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/28/king-charles-confirms-he-will-discuss-legacy-of-slavery-at-commonwealth-summit\">Continue reading...</a>",
